<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Learn — targum</title>
{% include '_icons.html.j2' %}
<style>{{ asset('reader.css') }}{{ asset('chrome.css') }}{{ asset('words.css') }}{{ asset('library.css') }}{{ asset('learn.css') }}</style>
{{ hebrew_face() }}
<script>{{ asset('theme.js') }}</script>
</head>
{#- `words` as well as `learn`: the panels, the list controls, the word table and the
    status pips all come from words.css, and the pip colours (--step-1..4) are defined on
    `.words` itself. -#}
<body class="words learn">
{% set here = 'learn' %}
{% set title = '' %}
{% include '_nav.html.j2' %}
<script>{{ asset('building.js') }}</script>

<main id="page" hidden>
  {#- How much of the language you have. First thing on the page, and a real count of a
      real thing rather than a score — §6: no invented currency. -#}
  <p class="known-line" id="known-line"></p>

  <div class="front">
    {#- The sheet (§13, 2026-09-11): the text to carry on with, drawn as itself — the
        reader, framed, at the place it was left, on the desk; under it the title, what
        it is, and one press. The frame is a picture of the reader rather than the
        reader (`preview=1`, and it counts nothing as read): a press anywhere on the
        sheet opens the text in this page. The one pure-paper surface on the page, and
        the brightest thing on it: the memory the front page protects is the text with
        its English beside every line, so the front page shows one. -#}
    <section class="carry-on" aria-labelledby="carry-heading">
      <p class="label" id="carry-heading">Continue reading</p>
      <div class="page-sheet" id="carry-sheet" hidden>
        <span class="card-cover" id="carry-cover" aria-hidden="true" hidden></span>
        <div class="page-window" id="carry-window" hidden>
          <iframe class="page-frame" id="carry-frame" title="" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"></iframe>
        </div>
        <a class="page-open" id="carry" href="/" aria-labelledby="carry-title"></a>
        <div class="page-foot">
          <bdi class="page-title" id="carry-title"></bdi>
          <p class="page-facts">
            <span class="page-english" id="carry-english" lang="en" dir="ltr" hidden></span>
            <span class="card-track" id="carry-track" hidden></span>
            <span class="card-meta" id="carry-meta"></span>
            <span class="carry-known" id="carry-known" hidden></span>
          </p>
          <span class="open">Open</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    {#- The conversation, on the front page and named as one (2026-09-11): "I can't
        really tell that it's a chat", "I should not be sent to a new page". It is the
        conversation page itself, framed without its bar, so what is typed here is
        answered here and a text it opens opens in this page. -#}
    <section class="talk card" aria-labelledby="talk-title">
      <h2 class="section-title" id="talk-title">Talk to targum</h2>
      <p class="section-note">Ask for something to read, ask about a word, or paste a link.
        targum answers in Hebrew at your level, with the English under every line.</p>
      <div class="talk-window">
        <iframe class="talk-frame" id="talk-frame" title="Talk to targum" src="/chat?embed=1{% if token %}&amp;k={{ token }}{% endif %}"></iframe>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <section class="read" aria-labelledby="read-title">
    <h2 class="section-title" id="read-title">Read</h2>
    <p class="section-note">Start something new, or see what came out this week.</p>
    <p class="weekly-line card" id="weekly-line" hidden>
    <span class="label">This week</span>
    <a id="weekly-link" href="/">
      <bdi id="weekly-title" lang="he" dir="rtl"></bdi>
      <span class="at" id="weekly-at"></span>
    </a>
    <span class="when" id="weekly-when"></span>
  </p>

    <div class="doors">
    <button type="button" class="door suggest" id="suggest" hidden>
      <span class="card-track" id="suggest-track" hidden></span>
      <h2 id="suggest-heading">Suggested</h2>
      <div class="card-body">
        <span class="card-cover" id="suggest-cover" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="card-what">
          <bdi class="card-title" id="suggest-title"></bdi>
          <p class="card-english" id="suggest-english" lang="en" dir="ltr" hidden></p>
          <p class="card-meta" id="suggest-why"></p>
          <p class="suggest-blurb" id="suggest-blurb"></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </button>
    <nav class="next" aria-label="What next">
    <a class="step" href="/library" data-door="library">
      <span class="step-what">Library</span>
      <span class="step-why">Scenes, the Bible, novels, news.</span>
    </a>
    <a class="step" href="/progress" data-door="progress">
      <span class="step-what">Your Progress</span>
      <span class="step-why" id="step-progress">Words known, days reading.</span>
    </a>
  </nav>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="panel" id="shelf-panel">
    <div class="list-controls">
      <h2>{% include '_fold.html.j2' %}<span>Your targums</span></button></h2>
      <a class="see-all" id="shelf-more" href="/texts" hidden></a>
    </div>
    <div class="fold-body" id="shelf-body">
      {#- What the word means, said once, where somebody first meets it. Not "a text you
          have built": most reading is somebody opening a text that was already built, by
          them or by anybody else, with its words already looked up. -#}
      <p class="note what-is">A targum is an interactive bilingual text, optimised for
        language learning.</p>
      <p class="note" id="shelf-note"></p>
      <div class="shelf-head" id="shelf-head" role="row" hidden>
        <span></span>
        <span>Text</span>
        <span>Chapters</span>
        <span>Last opened</span>
        <span></span>
      </div>
      <ul class="books shelf-rows" id="library-list"></ul>
      <p class="empty" id="shelf-empty" hidden></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {#- Everything you are learning, on the page you land on. Both lists were on Your
      Progress, which put half of learning next to the charts. -#}
  <section class="panel">
    <div class="list-controls">
      <h2>{% include '_fold.html.j2' %}<span id="words-title">Your Words</span></button></h2>
      {#- Which language the meanings are in. Drawn only for somebody who has meanings in
          more than one, the same way the language switcher is: a control with one answer
          in it is only a question nobody asked. -#}
      <div class="langs quiet" id="meaning-langs" role="tablist"
           aria-label="Definition language" hidden></div>
      <input type="search" id="search" placeholder="Search a word or a meaning" spellcheck="false">
      <select id="status-filter" aria-label="Filter by how well you know them">
        <option value="learning">Still learning</option>
        <option value="all">All</option>
        <option value="1">1 · just met</option>
        <option value="2">2 · getting there</option>
        <option value="3">3 · nearly there</option>
        <option value="9">Known</option>
        <option value="0">Ignored</option>
      </select>
      {#- Hidden until sync says there is an account to export from. -#}
      <button type="button" id="export-words" hidden>Export</button>
      <a class="see-all" id="words-more" href="/words" hidden></a>
    </div>
    <div class="fold-body" id="words-body">
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table class="rows" id="word-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Word</th>
            <th scope="col">Dictionary form</th>
            <th scope="col">Meaning</th>
            <th scope="col">How common</th>
            <th scope="col">How well</th>
            <th scope="col">Kept</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody id="word-rows"></tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="empty" id="words-empty" hidden></p>
    <button type="button" class="more" id="more" hidden></button>
    </div>
  </section>

  {#- Words you may already know (2026-09-10, targum-internal#245). A reader who reads
      Hebrew already arrives with a ledger of nothing, and the level is a real count of
      known words: rather than a level they could claim, the commonest words they have
      not met, fifty at a time, with "I know all of these" — every mark a real known
      word, so the count rises because it should. Hebrew only, drawn by `claim.js`,
      and hidden until it has rows to show. -#}
  <section class="panel claim" id="claim-panel" hidden>
    <h2>Words you may already know</h2>
    <p class="note">The commonest words of modern Hebrew that are not on your ledger yet.
      Mark the page you know and the next fifty come up.</p>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table class="rows" id="claim-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Word</th>
            <th scope="col">Meaning</th>
            <th scope="col">How common</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody id="claim-rows"></tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div class="claim-actions">
      <button type="button" class="claim-yes" id="claim-yes">I know all of these</button>
      <button type="button" class="claim-no" id="claim-no">Not these</button>
      <span class="claim-said" id="claim-said"></span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="panel">
    <div class="list-controls">
      <h2>{% include '_fold.html.j2' %}<span id="phrases-title">Your Phrases</span></button></h2>
      <button type="button" id="export-phrases" hidden>Export</button>
      <a class="see-all" id="phrases-more" href="/phrases" hidden></a>
    </div>
    <div class="fold-body" id="phrases-body">
      <p class="note">Phrases stay with the text they came from.</p>
      <div id="phrase-list"></div>
      <p class="empty" id="phrases-empty" hidden>Nothing yet. Drag across words while reading.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {#- Only there when there is something in it. -#}
  <section class="panel trash" id="trash-panel" hidden>
    <h2>Trash</h2>
    <p class="note">Kept for seven days.</p>
    <ul class="books" id="trash-list"></ul>
  </section>
</main>

{#- The first thing a new reader sees, so it is the onboarding now. It points at the
    Library rather than at the upload form, which is the whole change. -#}
<section class="nothing" id="nothing" hidden>
  <p class="lede">Nothing here yet.</p>
  <p>Pick something from <a href="/library">Library</a>.</p>
  <p class="hint">Or <a href="/add">add your own</a>.</p>
</section>

{% include '_foot.html.j2' %}

<script>
window.TARGUM_KEY = "{{ token }}";
window.TARGUM_INTO = {{ into|tojson }};
window.TARGUM_LANGUAGES = { {% for code, name in languages %}"{{ code }}": "{{ name }}"{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %} };
window.TARGUM_CATALOGUE = {{ catalogue|tojson }};
window.TARGUM_WEEKLY = {{ weekly|tojson }};
</script>
<script>{{ asset('charts.js') }}</script>
<script>{{ asset('lang.js') }}</script>
<script>{{ asset('vocab.js') }}</script>
<script>{{ asset('lists.js') }}</script>
<script>{{ asset('sync.js') }}</script>
<script>{{ asset('account.js') }}</script>
<script>{{ asset('covers.js') }}</script>
<script>{{ asset('shelf.js') }}</script>
<script>{{ asset('scenes.js') }}</script>
<script>{{ asset('learn.js') }}</script>
<script>{{ asset('claim.js') }}</script>
</body>
</html>
